---
// How a push to main reaches the server. Keep this in step with
// .github/workflows/build-image.yaml, .github/workflows/deploy.yaml,
// Dockerfile, and docs/deployment.md. Leave out hostnames, users,
// secret names, and the Docker Hub image name.
const steps = [
  { title: "Push to main", detail: "starts the build" },
  { title: "Build the image", detail: "Astro site in NGINX" },
  { title: "Publish the image", detail: "tagged latest" },
  { title: "Pull the image", detail: "docker compose pull" },
  { title: "Restart the container", detail: "docker compose up -d" },
];
---

<section class="deploy" aria-labelledby="deploy-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="deploy-title">How it deploys</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="deploy-intro">
    Two GitHub Actions workflows take a change from <code>main</code> to the server.
    The first builds and publishes the image. The second runs only after a successful
    build and tells the server to update.
  </p>
  <div class="deploy-layout">
    <figure class="deploy-figure">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 360 560"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby="deploy-svg-title deploy-svg-desc"
      >
        <title id="deploy-svg-title">Deployment diagram</title>
        <desc id="deploy-svg-desc">
          In GitHub Actions, a push to main builds the image. The image is
          published to Docker Hub. After a successful build, GitHub Actions
          connects to the VPS over SSH. The VPS pulls the image from Docker Hub
          and restarts the container. Each step is described in the list that
          follows.
        </desc>

        <g class="zone">
          <rect x="4" y="4" width="272" height="196"></rect>
          <text x="20" y="27">GitHub Actions</text>
          <rect x="4" y="236" width="272" height="90"></rect>
          <text x="20" y="259">Docker Hub</text>
          <rect x="4" y="362" width="272" height="194"></rect>
          <text x="20" y="385">VPS</text>
        </g>

        <g class="flow">
          <path d="M140 92 V120"></path>
          <path d="M140 184 V262"></path>
          <path d="M140 312 V388"></path>
          <path d="M140 444 V476"></path>
        </g>
        <g class="head">
          <path d="M134 120 L140 128 L146 120 Z"></path>
          <path d="M134 262 L140 270 L146 262 Z"></path>
          <path d="M134 388 L140 396 L146 388 Z"></path>
          <path d="M134 476 L140 484 L146 476 Z"></path>
        </g>
        <g class="flow-label">
          <text x="150" y="226">push</text>
          <text x="150" y="354">pull</text>
        </g>

        <path class="ssh" d="M260 156 H322 V420 H270"></path>
        <path class="ssh-head" d="M270 414 L262 420 L270 426 Z"></path>
        <text class="ssh-label" x="342" y="292">SSH</text>

        {
          [
            { y: 40, h: 52 },
            { y: 128, h: 56 },
            { y: 270, h: 42 },
            { y: 396, h: 48 },
            { y: 484, h: 56 },
          ].map((box, index) => {
            const step = steps[index];
            const middle = box.y + box.h / 2;
            return (
              <g class="step">
                <rect x="20" y={box.y} width="240" height={box.h} />
                <rect
                  class="badge"
                  x="32"
                  y={middle - 12}
                  width="24"
                  height="24"
                />
                <text class="badge-text" x="44" y={middle + 5}>
                  {index + 1}
                </text>
                <text class="step-title" x="68" y={middle - 2}>
                  {step.title}
                </text>
                <text class="step-detail" x="68" y={middle + 15}>
                  {step.detail}
                </text>
              </g>
            );
          })
        }
      </svg>
    </figure>

    <ol class="deploy-steps">
      <li>
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">1</span> Push to <code>main</code></h3>
        <p>
          Pushing or merging to <code>main</code> starts the build workflow. If a
          newer push arrives mid-build, the older build is cancelled so it can’t overwrite
          the newer image.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">2</span> Build the image</h3>
        <p>
          GitHub Actions checks out the source and builds the Dockerfile in two
          stages. Node.js and pnpm install dependencies and run the Astro build,
          then the generated pages are copied into an NGINX image. Only the
          NGINX stage is shipped.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">3</span> Publish to Docker Hub</h3>
        <p>
          The workflow signs in to Docker Hub with an access token and pushes
          the image, replacing the <code>latest</code> tag. The image is public, so
          the server pulls it without registry credentials.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">4</span> Pull on the server</h3>
        <p>
          When the build succeeds, a second workflow connects to the VPS over
          SSH, checking the server’s known host key, and runs <code
            >docker compose pull</code
          >. A failed or cancelled build never gets here, and a failed pull
          stops before anything is replaced.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><span aria-hidden="true">5</span> Restart the container</h3>
        <p>
          <code>docker compose up -d</code> replaces the running container with one
          from the new image. A reverse proxy on the server handles HTTPS and keeps
          running throughout.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <aside class="deploy-note" aria-labelledby="deploy-tradeoff-title">
    <h3 id="deploy-tradeoff-title">The tradeoff</h3>
    <div>
      <p>
        The old container stops before the new one starts, so the site can be
        unavailable for a moment during each deployment. There are no health
        checks or automatic rollback; to undo a release, I revert the change and
        push again. That’s fine for a personal site, and smoother deployments
        are something I’d like to explore.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the story behind this setup, read <a href="/blog/website/"
          >Making my website easier to manage</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  .deploy {
    margin-top: 80px;
  }

  .deploy-intro {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 32px 0 0;
  }

  .deploy-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 360px) minmax(0, 65ch);
    gap: 48px 64px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .deploy-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .deploy-figure svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .zone rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .zone text,
  .ssh-label,
  .flow-label text {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font:
      12px ui-monospace,
      monospace;
  }

  .step rect {
    fill: var(--paper);
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .step .badge {
    fill: var(--green);
  }

  .badge-text {
    fill: var(--ink);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .step-title {
    fill: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .step-detail {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font:
      12px ui-monospace,
      monospace;
  }

  .flow path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .head path {
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .ssh {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--green-deep);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 4;
  }

  .ssh-head {
    fill: var(--green-deep);
  }

  .ssh-label {
    fill: var(--green-deep);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .deploy-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .deploy-steps li {
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .deploy-steps h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .deploy-steps h3 span {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: none;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--green);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .deploy-steps p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .deploy code {
    background: var(--green);
    padding: 2px 4px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .deploy-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 360px) minmax(0, 65ch);
    gap: 16px 64px;
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    border: var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .deploy-note h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(25px, 2.6vw, 36px);
  }

  .deploy-note p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .deploy-layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .deploy-figure {
      max-width: 360px;
    }

    .deploy-note {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .deploy {
      margin-top: 56px;
    }

    .deploy-intro {
      margin-top: 24px;
    }

    .deploy-note {
      padding: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
